# Generated
build/
dist/
Run/*
config/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# where tools/build_openal_mac.sh fetches and builds OpenAL Soft
vendor/build-openal/

# The original game.  What the port runs on is committed so a clone builds
# and plays with nothing else to find: the levels and the level list, the
# playlists, the sounds, the four menu sounds, and the More games page the
# About screen reads - and the arm64 binary, which the disassembler reads.
# Artwork, the nibs, the video, the VoiceOver prompts and the code signature
# are not: nothing here needs them.
reference/*
!reference/Nightjar_arm64
!reference/Payload/
reference/Payload/*
!reference/Payload/The Nightjar.app/
reference/Payload/The Nightjar.app/*
!reference/Payload/The Nightjar.app/Exports/
!reference/Payload/The Nightjar.app/meta/
!reference/Payload/The Nightjar.app/nightjar_sounds/
!reference/Payload/The Nightjar.app/*.wav
!reference/Payload/The Nightjar.app/messagesList.plist
!reference/Payload/The Nightjar.app/objectsList.plist
!reference/Payload/The Nightjar.app/html/
reference/Payload/The Nightjar.app/html/*
!reference/Payload/The Nightjar.app/html/othergames_nj1.html

# the working brief (this machine's folders and the tester's details)
NIGHTJAR_PORT_BRIEF.md

# A third-party service's user names and passwords ship inside the original
# bundle.  Never commit it, never ship it in a build, never paste it anywhere.
# This rule comes last so no negation above can bring it back.
EIGC_Users.plist
**/EIGC_Users.plist

# Derived from the original binary and regenerable with the scripts in tools/
# (tools/psdis.py).  The HRTF table is the exception: it is committed, so
# nobody needs the binary to build.
tools/dis/
tools/classdump.txt

# what a self-test run from source writes
selftest.txt
selftest-update.txt
